INT. NIGHT FERRY - OBSERVATION DECK - NIGHT

Open air, plastic benches, a vending machine blinking in the corner. The engine thrums underfoot. Black water, white wake.

DAHLIA OYELARAN (30s, peacoat, a half-eaten sandwich) leans on the rail. Her ex, RUSSELL KAPLAN (30s, scarf, hands in pockets), stands three feet away, as close as he dares.

Below them on the car deck, two figures drift between vehicles: INGRID SOLBERG (60s, captain's cap, a flashlight) and her deckhand, BASIL MWANGI (20s, orange vest, earbuds).

DAHLIA
You followed me.

RUSSELL
I took the same boat.

DAHLIA
At midnight.

RUSSELL
It was the last one.

DAHLIA
It's always the last one with you.

He laughs once, short. She doesn't. The ferry horn blows.

RUSSELL
I got the job in Tallinn.

DAHLIA
Good for you.

RUSSELL
I turned it down.

DAHLIA
Why?

RUSSELL
You know why.

DAHLIA
I don't.

RUSSELL
Dahlia.

DAHLIA
Say it.

RUSSELL
Because you're here.

She turns. Wind in her hair. He steps closer.

DAHLIA
Four years, Russell. Four.

RUSSELL
I counted every one.

DAHLIA
You counted?

RUSSELL
Like a prisoner.

She looks at him, then at the water, then back.

DAHLIA
I almost called you in February.

RUSSELL
What stopped you?

DAHLIA
The phone.

RUSSELL
It was broken?

DAHLIA
It was mine.

He grins in spite of himself. She does too. A small, reluctant thaw.

RUSSELL
I love you. Still. Dumb, isn't it?

DAHLIA
Very.

RUSSELL
(hopeful)
But?

DAHLIA
But nothing.

She takes his hand. A beat. Then Ingrid's voice cuts through the PA.

INGRID (V.O.)
(over loudspeaker)
Attention passengers. We will dock in ten minutes.

BASIL (V.O.)
(over loudspeaker, muffled)
Also, someone left a sandwich on bench seven.

DAHLIA
That's mine.

RUSSELL
You're going to leave it?

DAHLIA
I'm going to stay.

He leans in. They kiss.

RUSSELL
^I want to tell my mother.

DAHLIA
^I want to tell mine.

They break apart, laughing, and she lifts her phone. His expression changes.

RUSSELL
What's that?

DAHLIA
A message.

RUSSELL
From who?

She turns the screen toward him. A name: "ELLIOT." Under it: "Ready for you at the port."

DAHLIA
I was going to tell you.

RUSSELL
When?

DAHLIA
Tonight.

RUSSELL
Dahlia.

DAHLIA
It's complicated.

RUSSELL
It always is.

He steps back. The ferry lurches as it enters the harbor. Lights ahead.

RUSSELL (CONT'D)
Who is he?

She opens her mouth. The ferry horn drowns her answer.
